// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: passed as a function-pointer
// A funcptr bound to a LOCAL variable and handed to spawn: the callback races a
// non-shared global, and the callback was never scanned.
//
// The spawn-arg funcptr scan looked the argument up in GLOBAL scope and required
// is_function, so a local binding fell straight through — while both the direct
// name form (`spawn w(bump)`) and the struct-FIELD form (fixed 5ed17c2f) were
// correctly rejected. Third form of the same question, third place it was asked.
//
// The local's initializer is now resolved to the bound function, mirroring how
// scan_frame already resolves an indirect call target for stack-depth analysis.
// Only a directly-bound `= func_name` resolves; anything reassigned or computed
// stays unresolved, which keeps this inside the per-file model rather than
// requiring points-to analysis.
u32 counter;

void bump() { counter += 1; }

void worker(*() f) { f(); }

u32 main() {
    *() fp = bump;
    spawn worker(fp);
    return 0;
}
